#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# gray_level

#% text
# `gray_level(g)` is the gray of level g, from 0 (black) to 1 (white).

#% text
# `gray_level(g, a)` is that gray with opacity a.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `gray` is `gray_level(0.5)`, `light_gray` 0.85 and `dark_gray` 0.25.

#% item
# Converting a colour to a gray level weighs red, green and blue by their brightness to the eye (0.299, 0.587, 0.114).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Five shades side by side:

#% cell
graphics(table([gray_level(k/4), rectangle([k, 0])], k, range(0, 4)))
#% output
#= image("gray_level.files/gray_level-1.png")

#% text
# The gray level of pure red:

#% cell
color_convert(red, gray_level)
#% output
#= gray_level(0.299)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `rgb_color`, `hue`, `color_convert`
